{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>They turn, but not upward</b> — the sense is: they return to Egypt, not out of need but only to slander their princes. This is the sense of <b>they are like a deceitful bow</b>, and the proof is <b>their tongue mocks</b>." "<b>their mockery</b> — it seems to me: the mem is a sign of 'men of the tongue.'"], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:32.786233007Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}